  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `ROADMAP.md` is deleted. It was a frozen archive since the Issue Law (2026-11-07) and lives on in git history and every tag up to v0.14.0: `git show v0.14.0:ROADMAP.md` (same as `DONE.md` before it, b6c39e6).\n- `AGENTS.md` Issue Law: says ROADMAP.md is retired, how to read it from history, and that no work goes anywhere but the issues.\n- `README.md` Project documents: the roadmap is the open issues; the archive is in git history.\n- `assets/ui/LICENSES.md` and a `Cargo.toml` comment pointed at ROADMAP.md M1.4.1 for the egui decision; they now point at `docs/spike-egui-go-no-go.md`.\n- `docs/decisions/41-retire-roadmap.md`: the decision and the audit.\n\nLeft alone on purpose: `RECOMMENDED.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, older docs (history), and the `specced from ROADMAP Mx.y` provenance comments in source (still true, findable in git history; editing them would touch every crate for no behaviour).\n\n## Audit: every open roadmap item -> its issue\n\nEvery row and bullet not marked done was matched. None lacked an issue, so none was filed.\n\n| Roadmap item | Issue(s) |\n|---|---|\n| Catalog 2D/3D Adaptive, M2.1, M2.4, M8.1 (trochoidal / constant-load, owed under M11.4 C) | #5, #6, #44, #47, #220 (open) |\n| M11.4 island late returns (round 6), ring fallback | #7 (open) |\n| M11.4 Pocket3D port, rotary wrap ladder, chord lag, arc fit, whole-model Pocket source | #8, #9, #10, #11, #12 (closed) |\n| M11.3 bore linear-lead dive, Rotary Parallel / Swarf entries, Rotary Offset, swarf leftovers | #14-#17 (closed); #48 (open) |\n| M11.2 oblique entries / Heidenhain vertical arcs | #18 (closed) |\n| M5.2 / M13.5 continuous C-axis live tooling | #33 (open) |\n| M13.5 G76 threading | #34 (closed) |\n| M13.5 ribbon reads `KindInfo::admits`, Setup pane offers the post | shipped in 7205935 |\n| M7.1 / M13.1 lathe lift, flute-rotation bound, eikonal | #19, #20, #22 (closed) |\n| M13.1 blade-profile sweep variant | #21 (open, in review) |\n| M7.2 / M13.1 dual contouring | #23 (open) |\n| M13.1 hidden-rest scan past its budget | #24 (open) |\n| M13.1 machined mesh facet highlight / deviation classes | #25 (open) |\n| M7.3 dexel retirement | #26 (open) |\n| M12.1 Solidcore kernel (and the M1.3 IGES + B-rep deferral) | #27 (open) |\n| M13.3 .iss compile proven | #28 (closed) |\n| M13.3 uninstaller signing | #29 (open) |\n| M13.3 Docker builds, wasm app/UI, headless binary per crate | #30, #31, #32 (open) |\n| M13.6 pocket/slot recognition | #35 (open) |\n| M13.9 fold annulus, reach ceiling, tilted shelf | #36, #37, #46 (closed); #212 (open) |\n| M13.11 2D Adaptive on a wide Outside band | #13 (closed) |\n| M13.11 G41/G42 wear variant, concave-corner check | #38, #40 (closed) |\n| M13.11 G41/G42 other mill dialects | #39 (open) |\n\nNot owed, according to the file itself: spindle efficiency as a `.mch` key (M13.2, \"not a promise\"), a cleanup ring around bridged holes (M13.11, \"if wanted\"), kinematics fidelity and a SolidWorks link (Open questions: out of scope).\n\nThis is the work tracked by #41. It does not close it: #41's original plan waited for every migrated issue to close, and the user retired the file before that.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
